.TH NORTHSTAR 1 "October 2026" "northstar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
northstar \- minimalist GTK 4 web browser with an original engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B northstar
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ URL | FILE ]
.br
.B northstar \-\-headless
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ URL | FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Northstar Web Browser is a web browser written from scratch in C, with a GTK 4
user interface and a libcurl network stack. Its HTML, CSS, and
JavaScript engine is an original implementation \(em it is not based
on Gecko, WebKit, or Blink. Pages render in the browser process under
a system-call filter and file-system sandbox; the browser supports
HTML5, modern CSS, modern JavaScript, WebAssembly, audio, and video:
MPEG-1, and MP4 or WebM files and Media Source Extensions streams in
AV1 or VP9.
.PP
When started without arguments, Northstar Web Browser opens its start page.
Passing a URL or the path of a local file opens that page instead.
A normal launch runs the browser under a small watchdog process that
restarts it, with its session, after a crash or a hang.
.PP
Any of
.BR \-\-headless ,
.BR \-\-dump ,
.BR \-\-eval ,
.BR \-\-act ,
.BR \-\-inspect ,
.BR \-\-inspect\-at ,
.B \-\-wpt
or
.B \-\-print\-config
selects headless mode, which loads the page without a window, prints
or writes the requested output, and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-private
Keep history, cookies, the HTTP cache and site storage out of the
profile on disk for this session.
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy= URL
Send HTTP and HTTPS traffic through the given proxy.
.TP
.BI \-\-window\-size= W x H
Open the window at the given size in pixels.
.TP
.BI \-\-gsk\-renderer= NAME
Select the GTK renderer:
.BR gl ,
.BR ngl ,
.BR vulkan
or
.BR cairo .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-watchdog
Run the browser without the watchdog process.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print the effective configuration and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-trace= FILE
Write a Chrome trace-event JSON file of frame phases, relayouts, scripts,
fetches and image decodes, which Perfetto or
.I chrome://tracing
can open.
.SS Headless options
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run without a window.
.TP
.BI \-\-url= URL
The page to load; a bare
.I URL
or
.I FILE
argument does the same.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump= MODE
What to output:
.B text
(the default),
.BR dom ,
.B layout
(the box tree),
.BR none ,
.BI png: FILE
(a screenshot),
.BI pdf: FILE
(the page as one long sheet), or
.BI print: FILE
(the page paginated as for printing).
Image and PDF dumps write a
.IB name \-initial. ext
file at the first render and the named file after
.BR \-\-time\-ms .
.TP
\fB\-\-viewport=\fP\fIW\fP[\fBx\fP\fIH\fP]
Viewport width, and optionally height, in CSS pixels (default 1000).
.TP
.BI \-\-viewport\-height= H
Viewport height in CSS pixels.
.TP
.BI \-\-settle\-ms= N
Milliseconds to let the page settle before output (default 200).
.TP
.BI \-\-time\-ms= N
Milliseconds to run the page between the first and the final image or
PDF capture (default 1000).
.TP
.BI \-\-eval= EXPR
Evaluate a JavaScript expression in the page and print the result.
.TP
.BI \-\-act= ACTIONS
Run semicolon-separated input actions before output, among them
.BI click " X,Y" \fR,\fP
.BI rightclick " X,Y" \fR,\fP
.BI type " TEXT" \fR,\fP
.BI key " NAME" \fR,\fP
.BI wait " MS" \fR,\fP
.BI eval " JS"
and
.BI evalfile " PATH" \fR.\fP
Because actions are split at semicolons, JavaScript longer than one
statement belongs in a file for
.BR evalfile .
.TP
.BI \-\-inspect= SELECTOR
Report the layout boxes of the elements that match a CSS selector.
.TP
.BI \-\-inspect\-at= X,Y
Report the layout box at a point in the viewport.
.TP
.B \-\-wpt
Run a web-platform-tests testharness.js page and report each subtest.
.TP
.BI \-\-wpt\-timeout\-ms= N
Give up on a
.B \-\-wpt
page after
.I N
milliseconds.
.TP
.BR \-\-debug [\fB=\fP\fILEVELS\fP]
Stream engine events to standard error. Levels are
.BR info ,
.BR warn ,
.BR error ,
.BR render ,
.B net
and
.BR js ,
comma-separated; without a list, all of them.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NS_HOME_URL
Start page.
.TP
.B NS_USER_AGENT
User-Agent string.
.TP
.BR NS_HTTP_PROXY ", " NS_HTTPS_PROXY ", " NS_NO_PROXY
Proxy settings.
.TP
.B NS_DOH_URL
DNS-over-HTTPS resolver URL.
.TP
.B NS_GSK_RENDERER
GTK renderer, as for
.BR \-\-gsk\-renderer .
.TP
.B NS_PRIVATE
Start in private mode.
.TP
.B NS_NO_WATCHDOG
Run without the watchdog process.
.TP
.BR NS_NO_CACHE ", " NS_NO_IMAGES ", " NS_NO_LOCAL_STORAGE ", " NS_NO_HTTPS_FIRST
Turn the HTTP cache, image loading, web storage or HTTPS-first
navigation off.
.TP
.B NS_SAFEBROWSING_LIST
Blocklist file to use instead of the user and bundled lists.
.TP
.B NS_LOG_FILE
Write the debug event log to this file.
.TP
.B NS_ALLOW_ROOT
Run even when started as root or elevated. For throwaway containers only.
.TP
.BR NS_NO_SANDBOX ", " NS_NO_SECCOMP
Disable the sandbox, or only its system-call filter. For debugging only.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/northstar/northstar.conf
Settings, one
.I key = value
per line; see
.BR \-\-print\-config .
.TP
.I ~/.config/northstar/safebrowsing.list
Additional blocklist entries.
.TP
.IR ~/.config/northstar/ ", " ~/.local/share/northstar/ ", " ~/.cache/northstar/
Cookies, history, bookmarks, site storage and the HTTP cache.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Northstar Web Browser exits with status 77 when it refuses to run as root.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project homepage:
.UR https://github.com/nordstjernen-web/nordstjernen-web-browser
.UE
